# Quantum-Sector Market Analytics Pipeline

**Status: In progress — actively being built.** This README reflects current progress and will be updated as each phase is completed. Code, schema, and results described below are partial; see the Progress section for what's actually done vs. planned.

## Overview

An automated pipeline that tracks and analyzes publicly traded quantum computing companies (IonQ, Rigetti, D-Wave, Quantum Computing Inc.) against broader market and sector benchmarks (QTUM, SPY). The project answers two questions: how has the quantum computing sector performed as an investable market, and does a quantum computing algorithm (QAOA) pick a better portfolio from that sector than a classical optimization approach.

The pipeline pulls daily price data, validates and logs data-quality issues, stores everything in a relational database, and analyzes it through both a statistical layer (R) and a quantum-vs-classical portfolio optimization comparison (Python/Qiskit).

## Tech stack

| Layer | Tool | Role |
|---|---|---|
| Ingestion & validation | Python (`yfinance`, `pandas`) | Pull daily prices, flag anomalies/missing data, load to MySQL |
| Storage & analytics | MySQL (hosted on Aiven) | Schema, window-function analytics (rolling volatility, moving averages) |
| Statistics & viz | R (`dplyr`, `ggplot2`, `forecast`) | Trend/volatility analysis, benchmarking, forecasting |
| Optimization | Python (Qiskit) | QAOA-based portfolio optimization vs. classical mean-variance baseline |
| Automation | GitHub Actions | Scheduled daily pipeline runs |

