## Database schema

```sql
tickers (ticker PK, company_name, sector, is_benchmark)
daily_prices (id PK, ticker FK, price_date, open, high, low, close, adj_close, volume)
data_quality_log (id PK, ticker FK, price_date, issue_type, note, resolved)
```

## Data source

Price data comes from `yfinance` (Yahoo Finance), free, no API key required. Because it scrapes rather than hitting a stable official API, it can occasionally break when Yahoo changes their site — the validation layer exists specifically to catch and log that kind of failure rather than silently ingesting bad data.

## Limitations (preliminary — will be finalized once the analysis is complete)

- Short trading history for these companies limits the statistical power of any trend/forecast.
- The forecasting component is intended as descriptive/directional, not a trading signal.
- At this basket size (4–6 assets), classical portfolio optimization is expected to match or outperform the quantum (QAOA) approach — the point of the comparison is demonstrating the method and when it does/doesn't help, not claiming a quantum advantage.
- This project is for educational/portfolio purposes and is not investment advice.

